{
  "title": "Gamification System: Achievements, Scoring, and User Progression",
  "introduction": "The Gamification System is a core component designed to enhance user engagement and motivation within the platform by rewarding various activities. It operates on an event-driven architecture, leveraging a points-based scoring system, badges, and user levels to recognize user contributions and progression. The system's logic encompasses event processing, score generation, achievement display, and configuration management, integrating seamlessly with other platform services. This merged cluster documentation synthesizes insights into the Gamification System, Badges, Levels, and User Scores, highlighting the comprehensive Gamification Logic and Achievement Display.",
  "core_functionality": [
    {
      "heading": "Event Consumption and Score Generation",
      "description": "The `GamificationConsumer` class serves as the central entry point for all gamification-related events. Extending `Msgr::Consumer`, it actively listens for messages published via RabbitMQ (Msgr) on a variety of topics, including `xikolo.course.result.create`, `xikolo.course.visit.create`, `xikolo.pinboard.vote.create`, `xikolo.pinboard.comment.create`, `xikolo.pinboard.question.create`, `xikolo.pinboard.answer.create`, and `xikolo.pinboard.question.update`.\nBefore processing, a global check ensures gamification is enabled via `Xikolo.config.gamification['enabled']`. If active, the consumer dispatches event payloads to specialized rule classes (e.g., `Gamification::Rules::Course::TakeExam`, `Gamification::Rules::Pinboard::UpvoteAnswer`). These rule classes are responsible for creating `Gamification::Score` records.\nThe `Gamification::Score` model captures details such as the `user`, `course`, the specific `rule` applied (e.g., 'take_exam', 'upvote_answer'), `points` awarded, and event-specific `data`. A `checksum` mechanism is employed to prevent the creation of duplicate scores for the same event. Scores are generated for a wide array of user actions, including taking exams/selftests, visiting course items, upvoting pinboard content, creating comments/questions, answering questions, and having answers accepted. Special rules, such as `attended_section` and `continuous_attendance`, also contribute to scores based on user activity patterns."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Badges and Achievements",
      "description": "Badges are digital awards granted to users upon accumulating specific scores for predefined rules. The `app/models/gamification/badge_types.yml` configuration file defines various badge types (e.g., `communicator`, `knowledgeable`, `selftest_master`), the contributing `rules` (events), and `levels` (e.g., 0, 1, 2 for bronze, silver, gold) with their corresponding score thresholds.\nThe `Gamification::Badge` model represents an earned badge, storing its `name` and `level`. The `Dashboard::GamificationBadge` `ViewComponent` is responsible for rendering these badges within the user interface, dynamically determining the image source based on the badge's name and level (e.g., `communicator_1.png` for gained vs. `communicator_not_gained.png` for not-yet-gained). Badge images are located in `app/assets/images/gamification/badges/`.\nThe system also supports integration with the Open Badges standard, indicated by `open_badges` configuration in `badge_config.yml` fixtures. This includes public and private RSA keys for signing verifiable digital badges, suggesting a capability for external issuance and recognition of achievements."
    },
    {
      "heading": "User Levels and Progression",
      "description": "User levels signify overall progression within the platform, achieved through the accumulation of experience points (XP). The `app/models/gamification/user_levels.yml` file defines these levels (e.g., `yellow`, `orange`, `green`), each with a `min_xp` requirement, a `title` (e.g., \"Yellow Belt\"), and an associated `image` (e.g., `kyu02yellow.png`). These level images are stored in `app/assets/images/gamification/userstates/`.\nA user's current score (XP) and level are prominently displayed in the global navigation bar and on the dedicated dashboard achievements page when the gamification feature is enabled, providing immediate feedback on their progression."
    }
  ],
